WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.971
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Saturday, October twenty fourth.

2
00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:12.590
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.603
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.603 --> 00:00:25.139
We start in Jordan, where gunmen opened fire at a Greek Orthodox church in the village of Hamoud, in Karak governorate, killing seven people, according to authorities cited by Reuters.

5
00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:32.364
The TRAC terrorism account attributes the attack to suspected Islamic State militants and reports at least twenty eight injured.

6
00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:38.799
International Christian Concern says the shooting happened during a funeral and puts the number of injured at thirty four.

7
00:00:38.799 --> 00:00:52.206
The State Department says security agencies are still hunting the perpetrators and have cordoned off the area, and the US Embassy in Amman says security has been ramped up.

8
00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:56.923
Canada and the UK have both updated their Jordan advice, and Canada says to expect a heightened security presence, including checkpoints.

9
00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:04.303
This incident could have repercussions for churches and ministries working in the region.

10
00:01:04.303 --> 00:01:13.834
In France, a gunman fired a submachine gun from a vehicle in the Paris suburbs of Trappes and La Verrière, killing one person and wounding several others, TRAC reports.

11
00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:17.872
Reuters reports President Macron called the shooting a terrorist and racist act.

12
00:01:17.872 --> 00:01:30.228
In the South Pacific, the US Geological Survey reported a magnitude seven point two earthquake in waters west of Vanuatu, followed by quakes of magnitude six point nine and six point three.

13
00:01:30.228 --> 00:01:33.911
That's preliminary information, and no casualty reports were seen overnight.

14
00:01:33.911 --> 00:01:43.787
In Kenya, TRAC reports al Shabaab militants ambushed Kenyan soldiers in the Masalani area of Garissa County, killing two soldiers and destroying a tanker.

15
00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:50.871
And in the Gulf, Reuters reports attacks on ships in the Strait of Hormuz hit a record high this month.

16
00:01:50.871 --> 00:02:01.291
ACLED says Houthi attacks are spreading beyond Saudi Arabia's southern provinces, with nearly a quarter of their attacks and attempted attacks since mid July aimed at oil facilities.

17
00:02:01.291 --> 00:02:03.288
A few updates on stories we've covered.

18
00:02:03.288 --> 00:02:15.075
Update on the Ebola outbreak: Reuters reports Kenya has recorded a second Ebola death, and Nigeria's health minister says Nigeria's case is linked to the virus found in Kenya's first case.

19
00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:20.236
The UK Foreign Office has also added new Ebola entry measures to its advice for the Seychelles.

20
00:02:20.236 --> 00:02:35.547
Update on Typhoon Champi: Reuters reports one person dead and five hundred injured in Taiwan, and the State Department says the storm is expected to pass near the coasts of Fujian and Zhejiang provinces in China today, with possible flooding and mudslides.

21
00:02:35.547 --> 00:02:44.386
Update on Tigray, Ethiopia: the Critical Threats Project says Tigrayan forces have reportedly retaken a town on the Eritrean border after Ethiopian federal forces pulled out.

22
00:02:44.386 --> 00:03:00.760
And on the protests in Europe: the State Department says the potential for demonstrations in major Italian cities remains high this weekend, especially today and Canada updated its France advice for demonstrations planned across the country this weekend.

23
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.951
Now a few quick notes by region.

24
00:03:01.951 --> 00:03:08.647
In the Middle East, TRAC reports two Israeli soldiers were shot dead at a checkpoint in Hebron, in the West Bank.

25
00:03:08.647 --> 00:03:16.424
In Africa, Canada warns that demonstrations may occur in Tanzania on public holidays and around October twenty ninth, and can turn violent.

26
00:03:16.424 --> 00:03:27.915
OCHA says the Democratic Republic of the Congo has reported more than fifty five thousand suspected cholera cases this year, with every health zone in Tanganyika Province affected.

27
00:03:27.915 --> 00:03:37.392
In Somalia, TRAC reports al Shabaab clashes with local militia killed seven people in Middle Shabelle, along with attacks on militia bases near Kismayo.

28
00:03:37.392 --> 00:03:42.558
In Nigeria, TRAC reports an Islamic State West Africa attack on militia forces in Borno State.

29
00:03:42.558 --> 00:03:56.254
In South and East Asia, TRAC reports the Baloch Liberation Front claimed an attack on a construction workers' camp in Gwadar, Pakistan, and a bomb disguised as a flashlight injured two people at a building site in Bengaluru, India.

30
00:03:56.254 --> 00:04:04.344
In the Philippines, two Coast Guard personnel were killed in an ambush by suspected Islamic State East Asia gunmen in Cotabato City.

31
00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:12.554
In Latin America, InSight Crime reports El Salvador indicted more than five hundred sixty suspected leaders of the Barrio Eighteen gang.

32
00:04:12.554 --> 00:04:18.306
Brazil holds its presidential runoff tomorrow, with public security a defining issue in the race.

33
00:04:18.306 --> 00:04:30.695
In Europe, Radio Free Europe reports the White House says a local cease-fire in Russian-occupied Oleshky, Ukraine, is set to begin October twenty ninth, to allow aid deliveries and civilian evacuations.

34
00:04:30.695 --> 00:04:37.526
And TRAC reports two arrests in Ireland after bomb-making material linked to the New IRA was found in County Louth.

35
00:04:37.526 --> 00:04:49.135
On cyber, Microsoft says a compromised release of the LiteLLM software package, version one point one zero seven point zero, could run malicious code simply when Python starts, even if the package was never imported.

36
00:04:49.135 --> 00:04:51.494
That's today's brief.

37
00:04:51.494 --> 00:05:01.181
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

38
00:05:01.181 --> 00:05:09.524
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

39
00:05:09.524 --> 00:05:11.682
This brief is digitally narrated.

40
00:05:11.682 --> 00:05:12.644
Questions?

41
00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:16.111
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

42
00:05:16.111 --> 00:05:18.330
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
